# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the Flask crAPI-style API (vulnerable code) in the
# background and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the API is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes the
#     "edited app.py but never restarted the process" case detectable (Python
#     does not re-read source per request, so the old code keeps serving);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the API cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART the API process, not merely start
# it if absent - it is already up with the vulnerable code.
